# sha256 pins for every binary the public build downloads.
#
# Computed on 2026-08-02 from the known-good dev site (../site, outside this
# repo) and then verified by actually downloading each source below and
# comparing. Nothing reaches a deploy whose hash is not in this file:
# .github/workflows/pages.yml checks each download before it is used, and
# tools/fte-web/upload-web-assets.sh checks the demos before it uploads them.
#
# Sources, and why each one:
#
#   quake106.zip  https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/ftp.idsoftware.com/idstuff/quake/quake106.zip
#     id's own shareware 1.06 release, from a mirror of ftp.idsoftware.com.
#     No mirror was found serving a bare pak0.pak that is byte-identical to
#     ours, so CI takes the canonical archive instead: pak0.pak lives inside
#     its resource.1, an lh5-encoded LZH archive that 7-Zip can read. Both the
#     archive and the extracted pak0.pak are pinned -- the second pin is the
#     one that matters, since it is the file we ship.
#
#   nquake.pk3    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nQuake/distfiles/d93997920e028343eee24377f75b2addff066990/non-gpl/qw/nquake.pk3
#     nQuake's own distfiles repository, pinned to the commit that last touched
#     the file rather than to master, which moves. Byte-identical to the copy
#     an nQuake install put in the dev site.
#
#   gpl_maps.pk3  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nQuake/distfiles/d93997920e028343eee24377f75b2addff066990/gpl/id1/gpl_maps.pk3
#     GPL remakes of the id maps, from the same pinned distfiles commit as
#     nquake.pk3. Load-bearing, not decoration: both bundled demos play on
#     dm3, and shareware pak0 has no dm maps at all (e1/start only --
#     verified by listing its directory). The real dm3.bsp is registered
#     Quake, and FTE's runtime map download is doubly dead from a Pages
#     origin: maps.quakeworld.nu deliberately hosts no id maps (dm7-9 yes,
#     dm3-6 no) and sends no CORS headers. This pk3's maps/dm3.bsp is the
#     freely-distributable answer nQuake itself ships.
#
#   *.mvd         https://github.com/Xerialen/ez-hud/releases/download/web-assets-v1/<name>
#     Our own release, because these two demos are not published anywhere else:
#     hudtest_src.mvd is a synthetic recording made for this editor and
#     tb4gf_book_vs_s.mvd is an openly shared match demo. Created (once) by
#     tools/fte-web/upload-web-assets.sh.
#
# Format is `sha256sum -c`: run it from the directory the workflow downloads
# into, where every file has the basename listed here.

ec6c9d34b1ae0252ac0066045b6611a7919c2a0d78a3a66d9387a8f597553239  quake106.zip
35a9c55e5e5a284a159ad2a62e0e8def23d829561fe2f54eb402dbc0a9a946af  pak0.pak
7295a0ee15370a47fdaf492ebf7479241b5b36554c32eb9be9330a234083e8b4  nquake.pk3
6e409cab705ea6046872383149a222fe76a351f03ac48055b3e5f1faaec9d6c6  gpl_maps.pk3
d9d2121e997e7980df3326dc1a91228c58aa523f56a843a152137f6c57871aa3  hudtest_src.mvd
45f653c08fbb5488e2619a24ee0dd71347316e60265b8e4caaff0f3607ce0f30  tb4gf_book_vs_s.mvd
